<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Limbourg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Limbourg is a small town in the province of Liège in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgium">Belgium</a>, on a rocky spur above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vesdre">Vesdre</a>. Its castle, built in the early 11th century, was the seat of the counts and later dukes of Limburg, who gave their name to the medieval duchy and, indirectly, to the modern Belgian and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> provinces of Limburg. The duchy passed to Brabant after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-worringen">Battle of Worringen</a> in 1288.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/limbourg.jpg" alt="Limbourg" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ArthurMcGill · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Place_Saint-Georges,_Limbourg_Ville_Haute_(2).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
